Definition: DBMS (Database Management System) is software that stores, manages, and retrieves data efficiently.

Types of DBMS:
Hierarchical DBMS – Data stored in a tree structure.
Network DBMS – Data stored as nodes and links (graph-like).
Relational DBMS (RDBMS) – Data stored in tables with relationships (most popular).
Object-oriented DBMS – Stores data as objects.

Advantages of DBMS:
Reduced data redundancy
Improved data consistency
Better security and access control
Multi-user access
Backup and recovery
